{
  "id": 442827403,
  "iid": 22929,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "wsutil: Get rid of HAVE_ checks in socket.h",
  "description": "socket.h is a public header, so (unlike C source files), so config.h\nmust not be included (d0a91b27f26762e9c998cc5e6fe71767de5d32c7)\nand thus HAVE_SYS_SOCKET_H and so forth is not defined.\n\nWe want to include everything necessary for Internet sockets regardless\nof platform. Right now that means Windows, or else UN*X. (The latter\nmay include Cygwin.) There's already a check for _WIN32; include all\nthe other includes in the else without checking HAVE_.\n\nSimilar to commit bfad9c56f9e65eafba00f97e5e649842782eb2e1, we might\nnot want to have a check in ConfigureChecks for sys/socket.h at all,\nand just have have files include wsutil/socket.h whenever they need\nsocket support.\n\nAlso, convert to 4 spaces and get rid of the modelines to match\nsocket.c, especially since the .editorconfig doesn't have an entry\nfor it so editors that use that default to 4 spaces instead of tabs.",
  "state": "merged",
